Given, $U=\frac{M}{r^{6}}-\frac{N}{r^{12}}\begin{array}{l}
\therefore \mathrm{F}=\frac{-\mathrm{du}}{\mathrm{dr}}=\frac{-\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{dr}}\left(\frac{\mathrm{M}}{\mathrm{r}^{6}}-\frac{\mathrm{N}}{\mathrm{r}^{12}}\right) \\
=-\left(\frac{-6 \mathrm{M}}{\mathrm{r}^{7}}+\frac{12 \mathrm{~N}}{\mathrm{r}^{13}}\right)=\left(\frac{6 \mathrm{M}}{\mathrm{r}^{7}}-\frac{12 \mathrm{~N}}{\mathrm{r}^{13}}\right)
\end{array}
For equilibrium position, $\mathrm{F}=0\therefore \frac{6 \mathrm{M}}{\mathrm{r}^{7}}=\frac{12 \mathrm{~N}}{\mathrm{r}^{13}} \text { or } \mathrm{r}^{6}=\frac{2 \mathrm{~N}}{\mathrm{M}}$
Hence, $U=\frac{M}{(2 N / M)}-\frac{N}{(2 N / M)^{2}}=\frac{M^{2}}{4 N}

We know that \(\Delta \mathrm{U}=-\mathrm{W}\) Therefore
\(\begin{aligned}
& \Delta \mathrm{U}=-\int_0^{\mathrm{x}} \mathrm{Fdx} \text { or } \Delta \mathrm{U}=-\int_0^{\mathrm{x}} \mathrm{kxdx} \\
& \Rightarrow \mathrm{U}_{(\mathrm{x})}-\mathrm{U}_{(0)}=-\frac{\mathrm{kx}^2}{2} \text { given } \mathrm{U}_{(0)}=0, \\
